{"id":"A1-L110","title":"S + V + O + complement: use","cefr":"A1","level":"A1","unit":"A1-U07","focus":"Subject + verb + object + complement — uso","targets":{"grammar":"Subject + verb + object + complement — uso","pron":"bed/bad","verbs":["hate"],"pv":[],"expr":[],"words":["neighbor","ugly","fight","beautiful","door","street","warm","smile"],"field":"Lugares","genre":"Conto e trecho de peça","skill":"Escuta","words_min":8},"frames":[{"tag":"Abertura","title":"Lesson 110 · S + V + O + complement: use","blocks":[{"type":"box","kind":"look","t":"Nesta aula","body":["**Foco:** Subject + verb + object + complement — uso.","**Verbos:** hate.","**Pronúncia:** bed/bad.","**8 palavras novas** (lugares).","**Texto do dia:** conto e trecho de peça."]},{"type":"p","t":"**Objetivo de comunicação (A1):** eu consigo usar objeto + complemento em contos e dizer hate."},{"type":"box","kind":"exam","t":"Ponte para as provas","body":["Você ainda não faz as provas, mas já treina o formato de tarefas curtas que elas usam.","Esta aula treina **ouvir e anotar informações (IELTS Listening, TOEFL Listening)**."]}]},{"tag":"Aquecimento","title":"Warm-up · Say the words","blocks":[{"type":"p","t":"Toque em 🔊, ouça e repita cada palavra. Depois tente adivinhar o sentido."},{"type":"words","items":[["neighbor","vizinho"],["ugly","feio"],["fight","brigar"],["beautiful","lindo"],["door","porta"],["street","rua"],["warm","aconchegante"],["smile","sorrir"]]}]},{"tag":"Leitura","title":"Reading · A short story","blocks":[{"type":"text","title":"The Red Door","paras":["Ben **painted the door red**. His neighbor **called it ugly**. Ben **hates fighting**, so he **kept the door red** and **made tea for everyone**.","At night the red door **made the street warm**. The neighbor smiled. “I **find it beautiful** now,” she said."],"kicker":"SHORT STORY","by":"A reader","gloss":[["neighbor","vizinho"],["ugly","feio"],["fight","brigar"],["beautiful","lindo"]]}]},{"tag":"Compreensão","title":"Did you understand?","blocks":[{"type":"tfng","title":"","items":[{"q":"Ben painted the door red.","ans":"T","why":"painted red."},{"q":"The neighbor liked it at first.","ans":"F","why":"called it ugly."},{"q":"At the end she finds it beautiful.","ans":"T","why":"find it beautiful."}]},{"type":"mcq","title":"Vocabulary in context","items":[{"q":"“ugly” means…","opts":["feio","bonito","velho"],"ans":0,"why":"ugly."},{"q":"“fight” means…","opts":["brigar","dançar","correr"],"ans":0,"why":"fight."}]}]},{"tag":"Gramática","title":"Object + complement: use","blocks":[{"type":"table","head":["Estrutura","Exemplo"],"rows":[["make + O + adj","**It makes the street warm.**"],["call + O + noun","**They call it ugly.**"],["keep + O + adj","**He kept the door red.**"],["find + O + adj","**I find it beautiful.**"]],"cap":"Object + complement: use"},{"type":"box","kind":"look","t":"Regra","body":"Verbos comuns: **make, keep, call, find, paint, leave**."}]},{"tag":"Prática","title":"Practice","blocks":[{"type":"gap","title":"Complete the sentences","bank":null,"items":[{"s":"Ben painted the door ___ . (red)","a":"red","why":"complemento."},{"s":"She calls it ___ . (ugly)","a":"ugly","why":"complemento."},{"s":"I ___ it beautiful. (find)","a":"find","why":"find."},{"s":"He ___ fighting. (hate)","a":"hates","why":"hate."}]},{"type":"match","title":"Match the word to its meaning","pairs":[["neighbor","vizinho"],["ugly","feio"],["fight","brigar"],["beautiful","lindo"],["door","porta"]]},{"type":"order","title":"Put the words in order","items":[{"words":["it","red","I","keep"],"ans":"I keep it red","pt":"Eu mantenho vermelha."},{"words":["ugly","I","find","it"],"ans":"I find it ugly","pt":"Acho feio."}]}]},{"tag":"Vocabulário","title":"Words and expressions","blocks":[{"type":"vocab","items":[{"w":"neighbor","pos":"word","pt":"vizinho","ex":"A kind neighbor.","expt":"Um vizinho gentil."},{"w":"ugly","pos":"word","pt":"feio","ex":"An ugly color.","expt":"Uma cor feia."},{"w":"fight","pos":"word","pt":"brigar","ex":"Don’t fight.","expt":"Não brigue."},{"w":"beautiful","pos":"word","pt":"lindo","ex":"A beautiful door.","expt":"Uma porta linda."},{"w":"door","pos":"word","pt":"porta","ex":"A red door.","expt":"Uma porta vermelha."},{"w":"street","pos":"word","pt":"rua","ex":"The street.","expt":"A rua."},{"w":"warm","pos":"word","pt":"aconchegante","ex":"A warm street.","expt":"Uma rua aconchegante."},{"w":"smile","pos":"word","pt":"sorrir","ex":"She smiled.","expt":"Ela sorriu."}]}]},{"tag":"Verbos","title":"Verbs in focus","blocks":[{"type":"verbs","items":[{"v":"hate","pt":"odiar","forms":[["I / you / we / they hate","I hate waiting."],["he / she / it hates","She hates fighting."]]}]}]},{"tag":"Escuta e diálogo","title":"Neighbors","blocks":[{"type":"dialog","title":"Neighbors","lines":[["Neighbor","I find it ugly.","Acho feio."],["Ben","I keep it red.","Eu mantenho vermelha."],["Neighbor","Why?","Por quê?"],["Ben","It makes me happy.","Me deixa feliz."]]},{"type":"pron","title":"Pronúncia: bed/bad","items":[{"label":"bed/bad","note":"/ɛ/ (bed) × /æ/ (bad): abra mais a boca no /æ/.","words":["bed","bad","men","man","pen","pan"]}]}]},{"tag":"Fala","title":"Speaking","blocks":[{"type":"speak","title":"Speaking","prompts":[{"q":"Say what makes you happy.","pt":"Diga.","model":"Music makes me happy."},{"q":"Say what you find beautiful.","pt":"Diga.","model":"I find the sea beautiful."},{"q":"Say what you hate.","pt":"Diga.","model":"I hate fighting."}]}]},{"tag":"Escrita","title":"Writing","blocks":[{"type":"write","task":"Write 5 sentences with object + complement.","model":"Ben painted the door red. The neighbor called it ugly. He kept it red. It made the street warm. I find it beautiful.","checklist":["Usei **O + complemento**","Usei **make/keep/call/find**","Frases claras"],"words":"5 frases"}]},{"tag":"Revisão e exame","title":"Review · Exam strategy · Teacher’s note","blocks":[{"type":"mcq","title":"Check yourself","items":[{"q":"What does “neighbor” mean?","opts":["feio","vizinho","lindo"],"ans":1,"why":"**neighbor** = vizinho."},{"q":"What does “ugly” mean?","opts":["brigar","porta","feio"],"ans":2,"why":"**ugly** = feio."},{"q":"What does “fight” mean?","opts":["brigar","lindo","rua"],"ans":0,"why":"**fight** = brigar."},{"q":"What does “beautiful” mean?","opts":["porta","lindo","aconchegante"],"ans":1,"why":"**beautiful** = lindo."}]},{"type":"box","kind":"exam","t":"Estratégia para as provas","body":["Treine esta habilidade com o formato de tarefas curtas das provas (TOEFL/IELTS).","Leia o enunciado primeiro e procure as palavras-chave."]},{"type":"box","kind":"teach","t":"Nota para o futuro professor","body":["Use exemplos reais da vida dos alunos e peça frases próprias.","Corrija o erro mais frequente da aula em grupo, sem expor o aluno.","Retome o conteúdo na aula seguinte com um exercício curto."]}]}]}